{
  "id": "fluency-l2-computing-limits",
  "lesson": "l2-computing-limits",
  "title": "Fluency: limits you can compute",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "cancel-linear-bottom",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "factor the top and cancel",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": { "p": "b - a", "q": "-a*b", "r": "a + b", "na": "-a" },
      "where": ["a + b != 0", "a + b != 1", "a != b", "a - b != 1"],
      "prompt": "Find $\\lim_{{x \\to {a}}} \\dfrac{{{poly(x; 1, p, q)}}}{{x{na:+}}}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{r}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "zero-over-zero-is-zero", "value": "0", "line": "Substituting gives $\\tfrac{{0}}{{0}}$, which is not 0. Factor the top and cancel first." },
        { "id": "zero-over-zero-is-one", "value": "1", "line": "Substituting gives $\\tfrac{{0}}{{0}}$, which is not 1. Factor the top and cancel first." },
        { "id": "sign-of-factor", "value": "{a - b}", "line": "Check the second factor: the top is $(x{na:+})(x{b:+})$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The top is $(x{na:+})(x{b:+})$, which shares the factor $(x{na:+})$ with the bottom.",
        "Cancel it: the limit is $\\lim_{{x \\to {a}}} (x{b:+}) = {a}{b:+} = {r}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cancel-two-quadratics",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "cancel a shared factor of two quadratics",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "b": { "int": [-7, 7], "not": [0] },
        "c": { "int": [-7, 7], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": {
        "na": "-a",
        "p1": "b - a", "q1": "-a*b",
        "p2": "c - a", "q2": "-a*c",
        "top": "a + b", "bot": "a + c"
      },
      "where": ["b != c", "a + b != 0", "a + c != 0", "abs(a + b) != abs(a + c)"],
      "prompt": "Find $\\lim_{{x \\to {a}}} \\dfrac{{{poly(x; 1, p1, q1)}}}{{{poly(x; 1, p2, q2)}}}$. Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{top/bot}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "accept": "${top/bot:frac}$, or a decimal within 0.0005" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "upside-down", "value": "{bot/top}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "line": "You turned the answer upside down: the top's other factor goes on top." },
        { "id": "zero-over-zero-is-one", "value": "1", "line": "Substituting gives $\\tfrac{{0}}{{0}}$, which is not 1. Factor both and cancel first." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Top: $(x{na:+})(x{b:+})$. Bottom: $(x{na:+})(x{c:+})$.",
        "Cancel $(x{na:+})$ and substitute $x = {a}$: $\\dfrac{{{a}{b:+}}}{{{a}{c:+}}} = {top/bot:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "difference-quotient",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "expand, cancel h and let h go to 0",
      "vars": {
        "k": { "int": [2, 9] },
        "a": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": { "c": "k*a^2", "r": "2*k*a", "t": "2*k*a" },
      "prompt": "Find $\\lim_{{h \\to 0}} \\dfrac{{{k}({a}+h)^2-{c}}}{{h}}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{r}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "square-split", "value": "0", "line": "You wrote $({a}+h)^2$ as ${a*a}+h^2$. The square has a middle term $2 \\times {a:()} \\times h$." },
        { "id": "factor-dropped", "value": "{2*a}", "line": "You dropped the factor {k} in front of the bracket." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Expand: ${k}({a}+h)^2 = {c}{t:+}h{k:+c}h^2$, so the top is ${t}h{k:+c}h^2$.",
        "Divide by $h$: ${t}{k:+c}h$, which tends to ${r}$ as $h \\to 0$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
